# React best practices

## Hooks

Call hooks only at the top level of a component or a `use*` function — never
inside `if`, loops, nested functions, or `.map()`:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function CatalogList({ catalogItems }: CatalogListProps) {
  return catalogItems.map(catalogItem => {
    const [isSelected, setIsSelected] = useState(false);
    return <CatalogRow catalogItem={catalogItem} />;
  });
}

// ✅ GOOD
function CatalogRow({ catalogItem }: CatalogRowProps) {
  const [isSelected, setIsSelected] = useState(false);
  return <button onClick={() => setIsSelected(true)}>{catalogItem.name}</button>;
}
```

Declare components and hooks at module level — never nested inside another
component, which remounts them and resets their state on every render:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function RepositoryPage({ repository }: RepositoryPageProps) {
  function SkillBadge() {
    return <Chip label={repository.repoSlug} />;
  }
  return <SkillBadge />;
}

// ✅ GOOD
function SkillBadge({ repoSlug }: SkillBadgeProps) {
  return <Chip label={repoSlug} />;
}
```

List every value the body reads in the dependency array of `useEffect`,
`useCallback`, and `useMemo`. Do not omit entries.

## Render purity

Render must be pure — no impure calls, no mutation of props, state, or globals:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function SkillCard({ skill }: SkillCardProps) {
  skill.viewedAt = Date.now();
  renderCount += 1;
  return <Card>{skill.name}</Card>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
function SkillCard({ skill }: SkillCardProps) {
  return <Card>{skill.name}</Card>;
}
```

Do not read or write `ref.current` during render, and do not call a state setter
while rendering — both belong in an effect or an event handler:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function SkillCounter({ skillCount }: SkillCounterProps) {
  if (skillCount === 0) setIsEmpty(true);
  return <span>{skillCount}</span>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
function SkillCounter({ skillCount }: SkillCounterProps) {
  const isEmpty = skillCount === 0;
  return <span>{isEmpty ? 'No skills' : skillCount}</span>;
}
```

## Effects

Do not mirror props or state into state with an effect — derive the value during
render instead:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
useEffect(() => {
  setSkillLabel(skill.name);
}, [skill.name]);

// ✅ GOOD
const skillLabel = skill.name;
```

Effects that start async work or a subscription return a cleanup so nothing
lands after unmount:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
useEffect(() => {
  let isActive = true;

  fetchSkills().then(skills => {
    if (isActive) setSkills(skills);
  });

  return () => {
    isActive = false;
  };
}, []);
```

## Module exports

A file that defines a component exports components only — named, never
anonymous. Shared hooks, contexts, and helpers live in their own file;
module-level constants may stay:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — helper export in a component file
export const formatRepoSlug = (repoSlug: string) => repoSlug.toLowerCase();

export function RepositoryRow({ repository }: RepositoryRowProps) {
  return <span>{formatRepoSlug(repository.repoSlug)}</span>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
const SKELETON_ROW_COUNT = 4;

export function RepositoryRow({ repository }: RepositoryRowProps) {
  return <span>{repository.repoSlug}</span>;
}
```

## Conditional JSX

Guard with a boolean — a bare number or string leaks into the output:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — renders `0` when there are no skills
{skillCount && <Chip label={`${skillCount} skills`} />}

// ✅ GOOD
{skillCount > 0 && <Chip label={`${skillCount} skills`} />}
```

## Checklist

- Hooks only at the top level of a component or `use*` function.
- Components and hooks declared at module level, not nested.
- Complete dependency arrays for `useEffect` / `useCallback` / `useMemo`.
- Render is pure: no impure calls, no mutation, no ref I/O, no setter in render.
- No prop/state mirrored into state via an effect; async effects clean up.
- Component files export named components only.
- Conditional JSX guarded by a boolean.
